# Ignore patterns for the dotfiles repo

# ── legacy / staged content under review (do not commit until reviewed) ──
scripts/legacy/

# ── runtime data (the *.db files live in /home/shared/data/ via symlink) ──
data/**/*.db
data/**/*.db-shm
data/**/*.db-wal
data/**/*.db-journal

# ── backups created by the migration itself ──
Backups/
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.backup
*.backup.*

# ── editor / OS junk ──
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp
*.swo
.vscode/
.idea/

# ── standard build / install artifacts (defensive) ──
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.cache/

# ── wallust-generated colours (regenerated on every wallpaper change) ──
# Derived from ~/.config/wallust/wallust.toml. A missing file here only means
# the consuming app falls back to its defaults, so none of these break a boot.
# Targets listed in wallust.toml [templates]:
#   cava        -> config/cava/config
#   kitty       -> config/kitty/kitty-themes/01-Wallust.conf
#   quickshell  -> config/quickshell/qml_color.json
#   rofi        -> config/rofi/wallust/colors-rofi.rasi
#   waybar      -> config/waybar/wallust/colors-waybar.css
config/cava/config
config/kitty/kitty-themes/01-Wallust.conf
config/quickshell/qml_color.json
config/rofi/wallust/colors-rofi.rasi
config/waybar/wallust/colors-waybar.css
#
# NOT ignored on purpose, even though wallust also generates them, because a
# fresh clone needs them to exist:
#   config/hypr/configs/WallustColors.lua      -> required by Decorations.lua:17
#                                                  (hyprland.lua:39). A missing
#                                                  file breaks the Hyprland config.
#   config/hypr/wallust/wallust-hyprland.conf  -> sourced by hyprlock.conf:5.
# To untrack those too, first make initial-boot.sh run wallust unconditionally
# instead of behind the .initial_startup_done marker.

# ── nwg-displays generated monitor config ──
# Hardcodes this machine's panel and mode; regenerated by nwg-displays on every
# Hyprland reload (hyprland.lua:44 -> require("monitors")).
config/hypr/monitors.conf
config/hypr/monitors.lua

# ── unused third-party cava shaders ──
# The whole directory is ignored. These are NOT wallust output (wallust has no
# shader template) and are NOT written by any script here -- they are
# hand-placed files, some MIT-licensed by rezky_nightky <with.rezky@gmail.com>.
#
# None of them are needed to reproduce this machine: cava's [output] section
# sets no `method` at all (so it defaults to `bars`), and
# vertex_shader/fragment_shader are commented out, meaning sdl_glsl is not in
# use and no shader here is ever loaded. Seven of these were previously
# tracked, which is not by itself a reason to keep tracking them.
config/cava/shaders/


